    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381">

                <pb facs="0579" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg485"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tyler to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Teheran, Persia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-16"><hi rendition="#italic">October 16, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Nov. 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 261, Dip. Ser.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Supplementary to my dispatch of the 7th
                    instant, transmitting correspondence concerning the state of disorder in the
                    city of Hamadan, <pb facs="0580" n="486" xml:id="pg486"/> I have now the honor
                    to inclose the reply of the Sadr Azem to my communication of the 2d of this
                    month.</p>
                <p>It will be seen that the minister assures me in express terms that the city in
                    question is now in a state of perfect order and tranquillity.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Tyler</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Vice-Consul-General in
                    Charge.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d381-a1.xml" xpointer="d381-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
